  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "S_xy[k] = X[k] * conj(Y[k])",
        "The angle of S_xy[k] is 2*pi*k*delay/size",
        "delay = slope * size / (2*pi), read from a line through those angles"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Why a slope and not a bin",
      "items": [
        "A delay in time is a phase that rises steadily with frequency",
        "The RATE it rises at is the delay, thus no single bin holds the answer",
        "Bins where the two share nothing carry an angle that is noise, and are weighed down"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What must be done first",
      "items": [
        "The angles must be unwrapped before the line is laid",
        "Each turn past pi would otherwise throw the slope out",
        "The answer is in samples, and farrow is what applies it"
      ]
    }
  ]
